{"notes":["minor: DELEGATION.txt sidecar is overwritten by name even when it pre-exists as a FOREIGN user file (classifyTarget returns overwrite; writeFileScoped replaces it) — contradicts README claim 'foreign files are never touched' (README.md:89-90). Overwrite IS observable in changes[] JSON. Fix: document the reserved filename in README/configure help, or refuse/warn when replacing a sidecar not produced by the pack.","minor: symlink refusal covers only the FINAL path component (os.Lstat in classifyTarget); intermediate directory symlinks (e.g. ~/.config/opencode -\u003e dotfiles repo) are followed via MkdirAll/CreateTemp/Rename. Acceptable for dotfile workflows, but install.go comments ('never writes through a link') and README ('symlinked targets refuse') overstate the guarantee — tighten wording or add an explicit dir-chain symlink policy.","info: writeConfigureFile (opencode.json / ~/.claude.json / ~/.codex[config.json]) still uses direct os.WriteFile — follows symlinks, no temp+rename, and silently resets the whole config on invalid JSON (drops unknown keys). Pre-existing behavior byte-identical to baseline 8626f95, out of diff scope; consider migrating to the hardened writer later.","info: nested walk paths p inside skills subtrees bypass safeName (only top-level skill/command names are guarded) — safe because go:embed entries cannot be '..' or absolute; keep this invariant documented if the embed source ever changes.","info: TOCTOU windows remain between classifyTarget (Lstat+ReadFile) and writeFileScoped (CreateTemp+Rename), but rename never follows a destination symlink and fails cleanly if a directory appears at the path — adequate for a local single-user CLI. No fsync before rename (crash may leave a truncated file; idempotent reinstall heals) and crashed runs can strand .ekapack-* temp files in user dirs.","info: expandHome does not handle the '~user' form — '--dir ~user/x' resolves to a literal relative dir '\u003ccwd\u003e/~user/x' under the codex cwd default. Usability nit, no traversal impact.","info: regression clean — pack.go verified line-for-line identical to baseline (install \u003ckind\u003e --dir plugin contract untouched); configure flag parsing unchanged; codex+commands refusal and conventional-dir layout change are intentional, documented (README/CHANGELOG) and tested; JSON changes[]/counts are additive; no new network/exec/privilege surface anywhere in the diff."],"role":"review","verdict":"approve"}